If the On-Board Charger (OBC) detects an HVAC input voltage frequency outside of the specified operating range, the OBC shall perform one of the following actions in order of priority:
1. Reduce the input power to a level within the specified operating limits;
2. If the input power cannot be reduced to a level within the specified operating limits, initiate the HV Shutdown sequence.

The proof of concept shall include the following four elements:
1. Documentation of collaboration with the supplier of the component identified by the antenna;
2. A complete set of simulations as defined in the "Simulation" chapter;
3. A demonstration of the specified performance values using prototype hardware;
4. Measurement results obtained at the vehicle level.

The component shall be equipped with at least three temperature sensors located at the following positions:
1. One sensor at the MOST FOT;
2. One sensor in the CD/DVD drive in close proximity to the optical pick-up;
3. One sensor providing temperature data for the HDD.

The Headunit shall provide an interface to connect to an external standard device to facilitate the update of the database. The system shall support the following update types:
1. Complete database updates.
2. Partial and incremental updates for the following data types:
    a. Map areas;
    b. Satellite and aerial imagery;
    c. Digital Terrain Model (DTM) data;
    d. Point of Interest (POI) data;
    e. Traffic Message Channel (TMC) tables;
    f. Language files;
    g. Software (SW) updates.

The system shall terminate the reset calculation if any of the following conditions are met:
1. A fast SOC determination is not possible;
2. A reset calculation is not required;
3. The determination process has completed.

The system shall execute the algorithms independently of the following driving conditions:
1. The alignment of the system vehicle relative to the preceding vehicle;
2. The acceleration of the preceding vehicle;
3. The deceleration of the preceding vehicle; and
4. The steering maneuvers of the preceding vehicle.

The system shall ensure that at least 75% of all objects categorized as "Ordinary" with a movement category of "Stationary" have the attribute `obj_ObstclDtct` set to `OBSTACLE` within 5 sensor cycles of the later of the following two events:
1. The object enters the ODA-Near zone;
2. The object becomes fully visible to the sensor within the ODA-Near zone.

If the PWM frequency remains outside the specified range for a duration exceeding the defined fault tolerance time, the system shall execute the following control behaviors:
1. Trigger a specific error threshold;
2. Display a predefined error message;
3. Maintain the specified temporal resolution; and
4. Apply the defined temporal correcting errors.

3. If the static control deviation (offset) exceeds the specified range for a duration longer than the defined fault tolerance time, the system shall execute the following control behaviors:
a) trigger a specific threshold alert;
b) display a defined error message;
c) maintain the specified temporal resolution; and
d) apply the defined temporal correcting errors.

If the position feedback unit's plausibility check remains outside the specified range for a duration exceeding the defined fault tolerance time, the system shall execute the following control behaviors:
1. Trigger a specific threshold alert;
2. Generate a defined error message;
3. Maintain the specified temporal resolution; and
4. Apply the defined temporal correcting errors.

The system shall trigger a warning if the following conditions are met simultaneously:
1. PPNM_ICCSOCWarnHybrid is equal to 1;
2. VehSpeedDisp is equal to 0;
3. ISPBatCurr is less than 0;
4. The conditions in items 1, 2, and 3 persist for a continuous duration greater than PPNM_ICCSOCWarnDebTmHybrid.

The sensor output pulses shall accurately represent the moving target teeth without any missing pulses or additional pulses, regardless of the following conditions:
1. Changes in rotational direction at any angular position;
2. Vibration effects;
3. Significant temperature fluctuations;
4. Transitions between stop and start modes (stop-start-mode) following extended stationary periods.

The system shall generate unique error codes to differentiate between the following three blockage conditions:
a.) a blockage detected after self-test or power-on;
b.) a far-range blockage detected during normal operation;
c.) a near-range sensor blockage that triggers a system state transition into "blockage" mode.

The system shall identify and process the following environmental elements as "complex situations":
1. Multiple crossing vehicles on multiple crossing lanes;
2. Multiple moving or stationary vehicles in the driving direction;
3. Oncoming traffic;
4. Standing infrastructure (e.g., guard rails, traffic lights, buildings);
5. Stationary objects located above or below the system vehicle;
6. Pedestrians; and
7. Bicycles.

The Front Panel shall include the following components:
1. One black plastic panel manufactured using foil technology;
2. One galvanised and laser-etched eject switch;
3. One disc slot; and
4. A minimum of [X] light guides.

If the interlock loop is open, the BMS shall distinguish between the following three error conditions:
1. Signal loop interrupted;
2. No HVIL signal;
3. Short circuit against LV+; and
4. Short circuit against vehicle ground.

The FPGA shall receive signals from SDCMD0 and SDCMD1 to execute one of the following three operations as defined in the software requirements:
1. Three-phase short upper;
2. Three-phase short lower;
3. Six switch open.

The design shall include the following 15 specific FCS operation points:
- Typical FCS operation points: points 1 through 10;
- Special FCS operating points: points 11 through 14;
- Stop mode: point 15.
